.TH NN-BISECT 1 "2026" "nn 0.1.0" "NN Manual"
.SH NAME
nn-bisect \- regression bisect over artifacts or git history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nn bisect [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find the first bad artifact or commit. {} in --test is replaced with the artifact path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-good PATH|COMMIT
Known good.
.TP
.B \-\-bad PATH|COMMIT
Known bad.
.TP
.B \-\-manifest FILE
Artifact sequence JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-git
Git mode.
.TP
.B \-\-model PATH
Model path in repo.
.TP
.B \-\-test CMD
Test command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 found; 9 test error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nn bisect --good a.onnx --bad b.onnx --test './t.sh {}'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
nn-regression(1), nn-diff(1)
